# Round XXIX Track C — `Dict.enumerate()` (DIRECT, no `.iter()`) rejects at
# check with `E_EnumerateOnNonIterator`. Dict impls `Iterable[T]`, NOT
# `Iterator[T]` — `.enumerate()` is an Iterator adapter (`lib/std/iter.gg`).
# Same class as the Set/HashSet reject added in Round XXVII Track D; the
# extension covers Dict/HashMap in `src/semantic/typecheck.rs`. RED at HEAD:
# builds (with C-emit warnings) and SIGSEGVs at runtime (exit 139).
# Post-fix: rejects at check-time; the fix-it advice `.iter().enumerate()`
# is the reference-grade spelling.
#
# The `#!` sha-bang and `EXPECT` fence direct the integration harness at
# `tests/integration.rs:build_gg_expect_fail` — negative fixture.
int main():
    Dict[String, int] d = {"a": 1, "b": 2}
    for (i, kv) in d.enumerate():
        print(f"{i}: {kv._0}={kv._1}")
    return 0
